.wikipedia.org/wiki/2002_Arras%E2%80%93Madrid%E2%80%93Dakar_Rally"}, {"title": "2000 Paris–Dakar–Cairo Rally", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2000_Dakar_Rally"}, {"title": "TOYOTA MOTOR SPORTS (DAKAR RALLY)", "url": "https://toyotagazooracing.com/archive/ms/en/dakar/qdr.html"}, {"title": "List of Dakar Rally records", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Dakar_Rally_records"}]}, "The search didn't find any record of a \"von Tell\" entry in the 2000 Dakar Rally. The only match was a rally in a different event:\n\n- **Michel von Tell** is listed on Wikipedia as a Swiss journalist, consultant, artist and racing driver. During 2000 Von Tell placed sixth at the Rwanda Mountain Rally in a Toyota. That was a Toyota result, but it was not the Dakar.\n- **2000 Dakar (Paris–Dakar–Cairo):** The rally was won by French driver Jean-Louis Schlesser and his co-driver Henri Magne in a Schlesser-Renault buggy. The EWRC car results page lists Toyota Land Cruisers in the field, but the snippet I saw doesn't include a von Tell entry.\n\nI couldn't confirm whether von Tell entered the 2000 Dakar at all. A full car classification from EWRC or the Wikipedia 2000 Dakar page would settle it."], "durationSeconds": 6.262208209000001, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01GCZ8T7JcLH4fbkNMBAvkLP", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
