tures-pirelli-star-driver-top-prize--608102"}, {"title": "2007 African Rally Championship", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2007_African_Rally_Championship"}, {"title": "2000 Rally Sanremo", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2000_Rally_Sanremo"}, {"title": "2000 Rallye Catalunya", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2000_Rallye_Catalunya"}]}, "The 2000 winner was Ugandan driver Charles Muhanji, co-driving a Subaru Impreza WRX. The event was then called the Fraternity Rally.\n\n- The rally's winners table lists the 2000 winner as UGA Charles Muhanji in a Subaru Impreza WRX. The official rally site gives the same name and car, and notes that Fraternity Rally · 2000–2001 was the event's name at that time.\n- A Kawowo article spells the name Charles Muhangi and calls him the first Ugandan driver to enter Rwanda Rally records with victory in 2000. The spelling differs across sources, but the win is consistent.\n- The 2000 event was also when the rally became part of the African championship.\n- Don't confuse this with the African Rally Championship's 2000 title, which went to Zambia's Satwant Singh in a Subaru, per the championship's champions table.\n- Separately, Michel von Tell placed sixth at the Rwanda Mountain Rally in a Toyota in 2000."], "durationSeconds": 6.657541958000001, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01KVsBMdvSEZuVGTJvWpniZc", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
